ms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1033 1474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5220265d-f52d-5c53-952c-690875cf1905" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186107942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186107943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186107944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186107945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186107946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107941 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107941 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107941 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1dc7909b-ed18-5a26-b360-ce0bd7c2f4b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107942 #edb/ref 1080 "\\log_{15} 48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107942 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107942 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d24b47a7-e7fc-5c9d-b197-a4155e4eb5a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107943 #edb/ref 1080 "\\log_{15} 12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107943 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107943 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "033f796e-65cb-527a-b376-9874d8dcb2df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107944 #edb/ref 1080 "\\log_{5} 10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107944 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107944 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3fe8fecf-db52-5bcd-8b48-8cb7b1c81ebc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107945 #edb/ref 1080 "\\log_{125} 48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107945 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107945 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "437705ef-eef9-5101-9c39-8b73ffebf345" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107946 #edb/ref 1080 "\\log_{5} 48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107946 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107946 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4d5fd34f-e06d-52d1-848c-edf3467c1c09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110486 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4014" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110486 #edb/ref 1071 "Express $\\log_3(2)+\\log_3(5)$ as a single logarithm." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110486 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4e63488a-97a0-5b21-ac91-2f0c9a1efa54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110486 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\log_n a + \\log_n b = \\log_n(ab)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule for logarithms, the given expression can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log_{3} 2 + \\log_{3} 5 &= \\log_{3} (2 \\cdot 5) \\\\\n&= \\log_{3} 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110487 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4015" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110487 #edb/ref 1071 "Express $3\\log_{5}{7}+3\\log_{5}{3}$ as a single logarithm." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110487 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "07d810ce-010c-5a07-8174-f01d9b807a60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110487 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\log_n a + \\log_n b = \\log_n(ab)\n$$\n\nIf we factor the given expression and use the product rule for logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3\\log_{5} 7 + 3\\log_{5} 3 &= 3(\\log_{5} 7 + \\log_{5} 3) \\\\\n&= 3\\log_{5} (7 \\cdot 3) \\\\\n&= 3\\log_{5} 21\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n3\\log_{5}{7}+3\\log_{5}{3} = 3\\log_{5} 21\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110488 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4016" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110488 #edb/ref 1071 "Express $\\ln\\left(x^2 y\\right)$ as a sum of two logarithms." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110488 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "679a8e3b-ef6c-565d-ab37-613dedfdf3df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110488 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the product rule for natural logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\ln{a} + \\ln{b} = \\ln(ab)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, the given expression can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\ln (x^{2}y) &= \\ln (x^{2} \\cdot y) \\\\\n&= \\ln (x^{2}) + \\ln y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110489 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4018" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110489 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\log_2(3)=k$ and $\\log_2(x)=p$, what is the value of $\\log_2(3x)$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110489 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "39a1c600-8d35-5671-bcb1-62682d750cd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110489 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\log_n a + \\log_n b = \\log_n(ab)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log_{2} (3x) &= \\log_{2} 3 + \\log_{2} x \\\\\n&= k + p\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110696 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110696 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110696 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110696 #edb/ref 1039 "Combining Logarithms Using the Product Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110696 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110696 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "0a5bab3a-bddf-54c8-a52f-1358f224c22c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110697 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110697 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110697 #edb/ref 1039 "Combining Logarithms With Coefficients Using the Product Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110697 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110697 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7f507303-8140-5228-8383-c27f2a7518af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110698 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110698 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110698 #edb/ref 1039 "Separating a Logarithm Into Two Logarithms Using the Product Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110698 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110488 #edb/ref